STEP 2 -- "verify show mirror reports no active mirror"                    FAIL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
x960-56YSQ#show mirror
  Mirror Test Port Name: port1.0.11
  Mirror option: Enabled
  Mirror direction: both
  Monitored Port Name: port1.0.10          <-- the ORIGINAL mirror, untouched and still Enabled

  Mirror Test Port Name: port1.0.11
  Mirror option: Enabled
  Mirror direction: receive
  Monitored Port Name: none (via ACL)      <-- a SECOND entry, added by the `none` command

x960-56YSQ#show running-config interface port1.0.11
  !
  interface port1.0.11
   switchport
   switchport mode access
   mirror interface port1.0.10 direction both
   mirror interface none
  !
                                           <-- both lines coexist in the running-config

  => STEP 2 FAIL: the drafted expectation "reports no active mirror" is NOT met. `mirror interface
     none` added a second, independent mirror entry rather than deactivating the first. Per the
     platform's own help, `none` declares the port a mirror DESTINATION whose source is selected
     by a hardware ACL (`copy-to-mirror`) instead of by a source port -- a different kind of
     mirror, not an off switch. The draft misread the case title. See the verdict block.

STEP 3 -- "prove the two entries are independent"                          PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: not in the drafted steps. Added because STEP 2's output is only interpretable if the
  two entries are genuinely independent rather than one entry being mis-rendered. The port-based
  mirror is removed, leaving the `none` entry alone.

x960-56YSQ#configure terminal
Enter configuration commands, one per line.  End with CNTL/Z.
x960-56YSQ(config)#interface port1.0.11
  % port1.0.11 is currently configured as a mirror-port. Use caution when altering its config
x960-56YSQ(config-if)#no mirror interface port1.0.10
x960-56YSQ(config-if)#end

x960-56YSQ#show mirror
  Mirror Test Port Name: port1.0.11
  Mirror option: Enabled
  Mirror direction: receive
  Monitored Port Name: none (via ACL)      <-- survives alone

x960-56YSQ#show running-config interface port1.0.11
  !
  interface port1.0.11
   switchport
   switchport mode access
   mirror interface none
  !
                                           <-- and persists as a configuration line in its own
                                               right, needing its own `no mirror interface none`

  => STEP 3 PASS: `mirror interface none` is an independent, persistent, destination-only mirror
     declaration. Removing the port-based mirror does not remove it. This also answers the
     drafted step's own aside that "the mirror destination config may persist" -- it does.
